<title>CANADA: Quebec 1997/98 budget figures and forecasts.</title>
<headline>Quebec 1997/98 budget figures and forecasts.</headline>
<dateline>QUEBEC CITY 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quebec Finance Minister Bernard Landry on Tuesday made the following forecasts in the 1997/98 budget: (Figures in billions of Canadian dollars, unless otherwise stated.)</p>
<p>				1996/97 1997/98 1998/99 1999/00</p>
<p> Revenues		    37.3    38.1    39.5    40.9</p>
<p> Expenditures		40.5    40.3    40.7    40.9</p>
<p> Program Spending	  34.7    34.4    34.7    34.8</p>
<p> Public debt charges	5.8     5.9     6.1     6.2</p>
<p> Deficit		     3.25     2.2     1.2	0</p>
<p> Total debt		  77.9     N/A     N/A     N/A</p>
<p> Total debt/pct GDP	44.1     N/A     N/A    41.9</p>
<p> Financial requirement   2.25     1.40    0.40  (0.85)</p>
<p>				 1996     1997    1998    1999</p>
<p> Nom GDP pct growth	1.9	3.1     4.5     4.3</p>
<p> CPI pct inflation	 1.6	1.7     1.9     2.1</p>
<p> Real GDP pct growth     1.2	1.5     2.5     2.4</p>
<p> Job growth pct	    0.3	0.8     1.3     1.2</p>
<p> Unemployment rate	 11.8    11.9    11.6     11.5</p>
<p> 90-day Cdn T-bill rate  4.2	3.7     5.0	5.2</p>
<p> 30-year Cdn bond rate   7.7	7.8     7.7	7.5</p>
<p>Note: Total debt includes direct debt and net commitments for public and parapublic sector employee retirement plans.</p>
</text>
